  "# OpenRouter provider application — awai.network / murakumo.cloud

**Status:** draft only; not submitted

**Hard hold:** fine-tuned artifacts, production inference backends, data policy, pricing, capacity, and reliability measurements are incomplete.

## Application summary

murakumo.cloud is applying to become an OpenRouter inference provider for Japanese-first models developed by awai.network. We fine-tune upstream open-weight models on a proprietary, rights-reviewed Japanese dataset. murakumo.cloud owns the public API boundary, authentication, routing, metering, reliability, and data policy. Baseten is the initial hosting primary; Together is a later fallback after access and identical-artifact verification.

The requested models are:

| Model ID | Display name | Planned base | Modality | Current state |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `awai-network/basho` | Basho | `Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` | streaming chat | artifact not trained; public route live but fail-closed |
| `awai-network/hokusai` | Hokusai | `MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3` | asynchronous audiovisual video | artifact not trained; public route live but fail-closed |

We will not describe a renamed upstream checkpoint as an original model. The prior Baseten deployment `basho-fp8-test` used `RedHatAI/Qwen3.5-9B-FP8-dynamic` only for infrastructure smoke testing and is not Basho.

## Organization

| Field | Answer |
|---|---|
| Model developer / publisher | awai.network |
| Inference provider | murakumo.cloud |
| Infrastructure vendors | Baseten primary; Together gated fallback |
| Provider website | https://murakumo.cloud |
| Developer website | https://awai.network |
| Contact and legal entity | OWNER-FILL before submission |
| Terms, privacy, acceptable use | OWNER-FILL public URLs before submission |

## Public API contract

- Basho: OpenAI-compatible `POST /v1/chat/completions`, streaming and non-streaming, with prompt/completion token usage.
- Hokusai: `POST /api/v1/videos`, job polling, optional signed webhook, and content download. Advertised duration, resolution, aspect ratio, references, and `generate_audio` are limited to verified capabilities.
- `/v1/models` advertises only ready models.
- Any missing endpoint, credential, health, capacity, price, or exact artifact-revision evidence fails closed.
- Vendor URLs and credentials remain private behind murakumo.cloud.

## Hosting decision

Baseten is the validation primary because this account supports custom deployments and `min_replica=0` scale-to-zero. Together's normal custom-model list does not currently cover the planned bases, while arbitrary Dedicated Container Inference requires sales enablement. Together remains a fallback candidate only after it serves the same immutable artifact and passes the same capability, health, capacity, and accounting checks. Primary order is remeasured before general availability.

Scale-to-zero is acceptable for review only if the cold-start path, timeout budget, capacity, and representative availability are demonstrated. An always-warm GPU is not claimed or required by this draft.

## Current production evidence

- Basho gateway: cloud-murakumo-api PR #194 merged at `3e91b9f507006493c71135d50be3ffcc4c52391e`; Cloudflare version `a9066a0a-c55a-4ebb-a690-d9de1eda7dde` is live on api.murakumo.cloud. A live unready request returns HTTP 503 `self_model_backend_unavailable`, and Basho is excluded from `/v1/models`.
- Hokusai adapter: cloud-murakumo PR #159 merged at `683cb6ed6eded3114be0b797eb259316e6f77e6b`; generated artifact PR #160 merged at `af0b6cb1d489e4babfe3a158af3e176f18c6136f`. After explicit owner approval, lease-free bootstrap deployed Cloudflare version `1b398be7-53e0-4683-9d75-009394080ed6`. The model page is live, and unauthenticated submit/poll requests return HTTP 401. The fine-tuned backend remains unconfigured and Hokusai remains pending.
- awai.network: network-awai-apex PR #1 merged at `174492d8186d62ae728c0f4f630a4af94fcf2310`; Cloudflare version `45d9a3bb-bff4-4a72-b06f-08b9aa629564` is live. Health and a real `murakumo-main` chat generation passed. Basho/Hokusai cutover variables are intentionally unset until readiness passes.
- OpenRouter BYOK tests against the existing catalog model `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` succeeded for Baseten and Together, but BYOK did not register `awai-network/basho`. Calling that unregistered OpenRouter model ID returned HTTP 400 `invalid model ID`.

## Pricing, capacity, and data policy

All commercial and performance values remain **未測定**. Before submission, provide Basho input/output USD per 1M tokens, context length, TTFT, tokens/s, TPM, errors and uptime; provide Hokusai USD per output second/variant, queue wait, generation time, concurrent jobs, success rate, artifact retention and uptime.

OWNER-FILL prompt/output logging, retention, deletion, training reuse, ZDR, processing regions, vendor subprocessors, and abuse/legal disclosure policy. Do not state `no training` or ZDR unless operational controls prove it.

## Submission gate

- [ ] Produce immutable Basho and Hokusai fine-tuned checkpoints and private artifact readback.
- [ ] Review upstream licenses and proprietary-dataset rights.
- [ ] Publish model cards, Japanese evals, safety evals, and supported-capability matrices.
- [ ] Deploy Baseten backends and pass direct positive/negative inference tests.
- [ ] Obtain Together access and validate the identical artifacts, or keep Together unadvertised.
- [ ] Pass murakumo.cloud streaming usage and video submit/poll/content/webhook tests.
- [ ] Publish prices, capacity, data policy, and representative uptime evidence.
- [ ] Fill owner/legal/policy fields and obtain owner review immediately before submission.

Do not claim either model is trained, generating, OpenRouter-listed, or generally available until those states are separately verified."}]
